---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: State and local class views
crumbs: [[null, "State and local classes"]]
---
{% import "macros.njk" as m %}
<h1>State and local class views</h1>
<p class="emst-lede">For state and local HR and classification analysts: civil-service classes from the pilot jurisdictions, with their minimum qualifications, licences and the EMST role variants drafted against them.</p>
{{ m.hrDisclaimer() }}
<p>Class specifications are linked, not copied: their reuse terms are unverified, so EMST stores the address, the retrieval date and a short paraphrase of the minimum qualifications. Only established core competencies appear in these HR views.</p>
{{ m.statFigure(emst.stateClasses.length, "Classes in the register", emst.figures.stateClasses) }}
{% for grp in emst.stateClasses | groupBy("jurisdiction") %}
<h2>{{ grp.key }}</h2>
<div class="emst-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="{{ grp.key }} classes">
<table class="usa-table usa-table--compact usa-table--striped">
  <caption>{{ grp.key }} classes ({{ grp.items.length }})</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Class</th><th scope="col">Code</th><th scope="col">Agency or employer</th><th scope="col">Spec effective</th><th scope="col">Draft EMST mappings</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for c in grp.items %}
  <tr><td><a href="{{ c.url | url }}">{{ c.title }}</a></td><td>{{ c.code }}</td><td>{{ c.agency }}</td><td>{{ c.specEffective or "not recorded" }}</td><td>{{ c.rows.length + c.pending.length }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endfor %}
